"""Micras main board, second revision: the micromouse's MCU, 4S power, DRV8874 wheel bridges, fan
driver, sensors, ESP32-C5 radio and debug probe, and user interface.

The design is research/next-revision/README.md: its design basis (DCX 10 L 4.5 V motors on a 4S
pack with no boost; no USB; the ESP32-C5 replacing the HM-19 module and the SWD connector;
digital 3V3_D from the L6981C33 and analog 3V3_A from a battery-side LDO; no 5 V
rail; the STSPIN958 fan driver at 400 kHz), its recommended options and its appendix connection
lists A.1-A.6. The blocks it keeps unchanged are boards/main's, with their designators; the
parts it adds continue each series, and the designators of removed parts are not reused.

This root sheet holds the STM32H725RGV6 (IC1) with its supply network and the test pads, and
connects the five sheets:
- REGULATORS (Regulators.zen): battery input, fuse, switch and measurement; VSYS; the 3V3_D
  buck and the 3V3_A analog LDO.
- DRIVERS (Drivers.zen): two DRV8874 bridges with their shunts and chokes; the STSPIN958 fan
  driver.
- SENSORS (Sensors.zen): IMU, INA241 current amplifiers, wall sensors with their emitter
  current sink, encoder slots.
- PERIPHERALS (Peripherals.zen): buttons, DIP switch, buzzer, LEDs.
- ESP (Esp.zen): the ESP32-C5-MINI-1 radio, debug probe and data link, and its flashing header.

The board's mechanics (outline, screw holes, encoder slots, fan hole, wheel and switch notches,
the drive blocks' zones) are spec/main2.toml. Its stackup and rules are boards/main's: the same
4-layer 1.0 mm JLCPCB stackup. Every part sits on the top side: the board rides 1.2 mm off the
floor (MicrasHardware Board.bottom_z).

MCU supply (DS13311 Rev 5; AN5419 Rev 3, Table 2 p7-8 and Figure 5 p10, "Direct SMPS supply"),
as on the main board, on 3V3_D:
- VDD (pins 9, 22, 35, 51, 68): C12-C16 100 nF, one per pin, and C17 4.7 uF.
- VDDSMPS (pin 6) = VDD: C1 10 uF and C2 4.7 uF.
- VLXSMPS (pin 5) to L1 2.2 uH (AFE201612S2R2MBT), whose other end is VCORE; C3 and C4 10 uF.
- VFBSMPS (pin 7) and VCAP1-3 (pins 33, 49, 66) all on VCORE, with C7, C6 and C5 100 nF at
  VCAP1, VCAP2 and VCAP3. The firmware selects PWR_DIRECT_SMPS_SUPPLY.
- VDDA (pin 16): from 3V3_A, the analog LDO, through R67, a 0 Ohm link in the place of the main
  board's ferrite bead FB1 (research Power tree: its 340 mOhm DCR times the ADC current step is
  about 5 LSB at each scan start), with C10 100 nF and C11 1 uF at the pin (AN5419 Table 2). On
  this package VREF+ is VDDA (DS13311 Figures 46-47 note 1), so the ADC reference is 3V3_A, to
  which the INA241 references and the emitter set-point are ratiometric. 3V3_A starts after VDD
  (its LDO's EN is on 3V3_D), so VDDA never leads VDD at power-up (DS13311 section 3.7.1).
- VBAT (pin 1): 3V3_D (AN5419 Table 2, no backup battery), with C8 100 nF and C9 1 uF.

Pin budget (research H7 pin budget): the two pins the main board left open carry two more
lines, Motors_nFault (both DRV8874 nFAULT wire-ORed) and ESP_Flow (the ESP32-C5's credit and
attention line).
Layout pin swaps (owner, 2026-10-20): the DIP switch sits on the STM32's right and rear, so
Switch_1-3 take the plain inputs on the right-facing pin rows, PH1, PC15 and PC14 (reduced-drive
pins, fine for inputs with pull-ups), and the lines bound for the rear-left leave from the
left-facing rows: Motors_nFault on PB2 (EXTI2); on the main board's pins every one of them circled
the chip. BOOT0 is held low by R42: the MCU always starts from its flash.
Layout pin swaps (owner, 2026-10-24), so that no line crosses the STM32's rear tip, where the VCORE
island leaves In2.Cu no room: the four wall-emitter selectors move from TIM4 (PB6-PB9, all on the
rear-right row) to TIM3, whose channels reach both sides: Wall_Sensor_PWM_0 on PC9 (TIM3_CH4) and
Wall_Sensor_PWM_1 on PB0 (TIM3_CH3) on the left rows, by their emitters, Wall_Sensor_PWM_2 on PB4
(TIM3_CH1) and Wall_Sensor_PWM_3 on PB5 (TIM3_CH2) on the rear-right row (PB4 leaves its reset
function NJTRST: the debug port is SWD only; out of reset PB4 is NJTRST with its pull-up, RM0468 Rev
3 section 11.3.1, which lifts Wall_Sensor_PWM_2's AC-coupled gate for a few ms while the emitter
set-point is 0, so no emitter lights). The left motor's EN stays on PC7 but takes TIM8_CH2, slaved
to TIM1 over ITR0 (RM0468 Table 350: TIM8 ITR0 = tim1_trgo) in gated mode; its PH (a GPIO) moves
to PC6. LED_ARGB leaves TIM8_CH1 for PB9 (TIM17_CH1, its CCR1 written by DMA on tim17_up, DMAMUX1
input 112, RM0468 Table 118). The rest are GPIOs: Motor_Right_PH on PB8, by the right bridge's
lines, Encoder_Right_CSn on PB7 beside the SPI pins toward its slot (EC1, on the right), and
ESP_Flow on PA9 on the rear-left row, toward the ESP32. The motor
timers: right motor EN/PH on PA8 (TIM1_CH1) and PB8, left on PC7 (TIM8_CH2) and PC6. The ADC lines
are swapped for the routing: Current_Sensor_Left on PB1, Wall_Sensor_0 on PA4, Wall_Sensor_3 on PC0,
Current_Sensor_Right still on PC1. Each pin keeps an ADC1 and an ADC2 input, which the currents'
dual injected-simultaneous sampling needs (PB1 ADC1/2_INP5, PC1 ADC1/2/3_INP11, PA4 ADC1/2_INP18,
PC0 ADC1/2/3_INP10), and PB1 is a fast channel (DS13311 Table 85; research Current sensing), so the
left current takes half of the research's fast-ADC swap.
Pin map check: the 46 I/Os of the VFQFPN68 are each assigned once, every alternate function exists
on its pin (STMicroelectronics STM32_open_pin_data, the STM32CubeMX MCU database: STM32H725RGVx.xml
and GPIO-STM32H72_gpio_v1_0_Modes.xml; PC9/PB0/PB4/PB5 TIM3_CH4/CH3/CH1/CH2 AF2, PC7 TIM8_CH2 AF3,
PB9 TIM17_CH1 AF1, PA8 TIM1_CH1 AF1, PA0/PA1 TIM5 AF2, PA15/PB3 TIM2 AF1, PA2 TIM15_CH1 AF4, PB15
TIM12_CH2 AF2, PC10-PC12 SPI3 AF6, PA12 SPI2_SCK AF5, PB14 SPI2_MISO AF5, and in the fallback
PA11/PA12 UART4_RX/UART4_TX AF6), and each timer serves one function (TIM1,
TIM8 motors; TIM2, TIM5 encoders; TIM3 selectors; TIM12 fan; TIM15 buzzer; TIM17 LEDs; TIM4 spare,
the emitter DAC's trigger). The timer, DMA, DAC and ADC set-up, with the RM0468 Rev 3 and ES0491
Rev 9 numbers, is boards/main2/firmware_changes.toml (drive, current, emitters, leds). STM32CubeMX
6.18.1 (MCU database DB.6.0.181, STM32Cube FW_H7 V1.13.0) loads that whole set-up as a project
built from the firmware's micras_v1.ioc with these pins, and generates its code without a
conflict: every pin's alternate function as above, TIM8 gated on ITR0 and TIM4 gated on ITR2,
TIM1 TRGO = enable and TRGO2 = update, ADC1/ADC2 dual injected simultaneous on channels 5 and 11
triggered by TIM1 TRGO2 with ADC1's regular group, DAC1 channel 2 on PA5 triggered by TIM4 TRGO
with its buffer off, channel 1 on-chip only beside PA4's ADC input, and the DMA requests of
ADC1, SPI2 (or UART4), SPI3, TIM17_UP and DAC1 channel 2, at the firmware's 550 MHz clock tree
(275 MHz timer clocks).
- The link to the ESP32-C5 (ESP sheet; firmware_changes.toml link) is SPI2 in half-duplex on
  three wires, the MCU the master (SPI_CFG2 COMM = 11, RM0468 Rev 3 section 55.4.4 and Figure
  643), its one data line on the MISO pad with IOSWP = 1 (sections 55.4.2 and 55.4.4: the data
  pins swap in any mode): ESP_SCK on PA12 (SPI2_SCK, AF5), ESP_DATA on PB14 (SPI2_MISO, AF5),
  ESP_CSn on PA11 (a GPIO output: software chip select), and ESP_Flow on PA9 (EXTI9), the C5's
  credit and attention line. UART4 is the fallback on the same pins, with no board change:
  ESP_SCK becomes UART4_TX (PA12, AF6) and ESP_CSn UART4_RX (PA11, AF6), the C5's UART1 behind
  them. The DMA requests are spi2_rx_dma and spi2_tx_dma, DMAMUX1 inputs 39 and 40 (RM0468 Table
  118). STM32CubeMX 6.18.1 offers the IO swap in half-duplex slave mode only: in master mode it
  puts the data line on the MOSI pad and rejects PB14. The CubeMX check therefore runs SPI2 as a
  half-duplex slave with IO swap, which places SPI2_SCK on PA12 and SPI2_MISO on PB14 and generates
  the SPI2_RX and SPI2_TX DMA streams with the rest of the set-up above, ESP_CSn and ESP_Flow as
  GPIOs, and UART4 on PA11/PA12 in the fallback project; the firmware runs SPI2 as the master and
  sets its IOSWP itself (HAL Init.IOSwap = SPI_IO_SWAP_ENABLE, firmware_changes.toml link_spi).
  PB14 left Fan_Enable for the link: Fan_Enable is on PB10
  (open drain, DRIVERS sheet), and the IMU's INT1 alone is IMU_INT on PB6 (EXTI6), its INT2 left
  open (SENSORS sheet).
- PA5 is DAC1_OUT2, Wall_Emitter_Set, the wall emitters' current set-point (SENSORS sheet). PA4
  (DAC1_OUT1) and PA5 are the package's only DAC outputs (STM32CubeMX MCU database,
  STM32H725RGVx; DS13311 Table 8), and PA4 carries Wall_Sensor_0: DAC channel 1 stays disabled
  and off the PA4 pad (DAC_MCR MODE1 = 011, RM0468 Table 266), and the ADC reaches PA4 through
  the pin's analog switch (ADC_PCSEL bit 18, RM0468 section 28.4.12).
- PC5 reads the battery voltage from its divider (REGULATORS sheet): ADC12_INP8, a slow channel
  (DS13311 Table 85 notes 4-5: on PC5 only the INN input is fast), on a TT_ha pin (Table 8) that
  the divider keeps below VDDA.
- PH0 is Switch_0, a plain input with the internal pull-up for the DIP switch: an FT I/O (Table 8)
  that takes no negative injection (Table 54), which a switch to GND does not cause. The firmware
  leaves the HSE off: there is no HSE or LSE crystal.

SWD header SWD1 (bare 1.27 mm pitch pads, not assembled), for an ST-Link when the ESP32-C5 cannot
reach the MCU (no NRST: the owner's choice), in the 4-pin order of the owner's clone ST-Link lead
(owner, 2026-11-01): 1 SWDIO, 2 GND, 3 SWCLK, 4 5V_IN. The lead plugs on pin 1 to pad 1 (the square
pad, with the footprint's pin-1 corner and "5V" at pad 4 on the silkscreen); turned round, or
shifted one pad either way, its 5 V never lands on GND, and nothing more is added to protect the
header (the owner's choice). Pad 4 takes the probe's 5 V pin, never its 3.3 V one: 5V_IN feeds
VSYS through D17 (REGULATORS sheet), so a clone ST-Link powers the whole board for flashing without
the pack, and with the pack in D17 blocks (VSYS 11.4-17.4 V). The probe's 3.3 V pin stays
unconnected: nothing on the header takes it. The probe's own fuse and lead drop part of its USB
VBUS before pad 4; at the lowest the buck runs at its maximum duty and 3V3_D follows VSYS at about
3.2 V, enough to flash (REGULATORS sheet, 5V_IN). The board has no test pads.
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Spi")
load(
    "@stdlib/board_config.zen",
    "BoardConfig",
    "Constraints",
    "Copper",
    "CopperLayer",
    "DesignRules",
    "DielectricLayer",
    "Holes",
    "Material",
    "NetClass",
    "PredefinedSizes",
    "Silkscreen",
    "SolderMask",
    "Stackup",
    "ViaDimension",
)
load("./passives.zen", "C_100N_0402", "C_10U_0603", "C_1U_0402", "C_4U7_0402", "R_0_0402")

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")
Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")
AFE201612S2R2MBT = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/magnetsyc/AFE201612S2R2MBT/AFE201612S2R2MBT.zen")
STM32H725RGV6 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/st/STM32H725RGV6/STM32H725RGV6.zen")
MountingHole = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/micras/MountingHole/MountingHole.zen")
SwdHeader = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/micras/SwdHeader/SwdHeader.zen")
Regulators = Module("./Regulators.zen")
Drivers = Module("./Drivers.zen")
Sensors = Module("./Sensors.zen")
Peripherals = Module("./Peripherals.zen")
Esp = Module("./Esp.zen")

# Supplies.
# 4S LiPo on J1: 12.0-16.8 V, 17.4 V with HV cells (research Design basis).
BAT_P = Power("BAT_P", voltage="12V to 17.4V")
# The battery after the fuse F1: the bridges' and the fan driver's supply.
VBAT = Power("VBAT", voltage="12V to 17.4V")
# Programming power: a USB-serial adapter's or a clone ST-Link's 5 V pin on J2 pin 2 or SWD1 pad 4,
# the USB VBUS it passes on: 4.40-5.25 V at a low-power port's connector, 4.75-5.25 V at a
# high-power one (USB 2.0 Specification, section 7.3.2, Table 7-7).
V5V_IN = Power("5V_IN", voltage="4.4V to 5.25V")
# VBAT (or 5V_IN, without the pack) less a B5819W's drop, 0.6 V at most at 1 A (JCET B5817W-B5819W
# p1), about 0.25 V at a light load (p2, typical; research Power tree): 11.4-17.4 V on the pack,
# 3.8-5.0 V on 5V_IN.
VSYS = Power("VSYS", voltage="3.8V to 17.4V")
# L6981C33 fixed output (DS13554 Table 6 p6: 3.284-3.346 V, TJ -40 to 125 C).
V3V3_D = Power("3V3_D", voltage="3.284V to 3.346V")
# ADP7142ACPZN3.3 fixed output (Rev H Table 1: 3.24-3.36 V over load, line and temperature).
V3V3_A = Power("3V3_A", voltage="3.24V to 3.36V")
# The ADC and analog supply, 3V3_A through the 0 Ohm R67.
VDDA = Power("VDDA", voltage="3.24V to 3.36V")
# STM32 core supply from the on-chip SMPS: VOS3 to VOS0 (DS13311 Table 13 p117).
VCORE = Power("VCORE", voltage="0.95V to 1.40V")
# SMPS switching node; AN5419 Table 2 gives its range as VCORE in the Direct SMPS supply.
SMPS_LX = Power("SMPS_LX", voltage="0.95V to 1.40V")
GND = Ground("GND")
# Battery pack minus, switched to GND by Q6.
GND_BAT = Ground("GND_BAT")

# MCU signals (names as in the firmware's pin map and boards/main2/firmware_changes.toml).
RESET = Net("Reset")
BOOT = Net("Boot")
SWDIO = Net("SWDIO")
SWCLK = Net("SWCLK")
ESP_SCK = Net("ESP_SCK")
ESP_CSN = Net("ESP_CSn")
ESP_DATA = Net("ESP_DATA")
ESP_FLOW = Net("ESP_Flow")
BUTTON = Net("Button")
BUZZER = Net("Buzzer")
LED_ARGB = Net("LED_ARGB")
LED_RED = Net("LED_Red")
SWITCH_0 = Net("Switch_0")
SWITCH_1 = Net("Switch_1")
SWITCH_2 = Net("Switch_2")
SWITCH_3 = Net("Switch_3")

SPI_SCK = Net("SPI_SCK")
SPI_MISO = Net("SPI_MISO")
SPI_MOSI = Net("SPI_MOSI")
IMU_SPI = Spi(CS=Net("IMU_SPI_CSn"), CLK=SPI_SCK, MISO=SPI_MISO, MOSI=SPI_MOSI)
ENCODER_LEFT_SPI = Spi(CS=Net("Encoder_Left_CSn"), CLK=SPI_SCK, MISO=SPI_MISO, MOSI=SPI_MOSI)
ENCODER_RIGHT_SPI = Spi(CS=Net("Encoder_Right_CSn"), CLK=SPI_SCK, MISO=SPI_MISO, MOSI=SPI_MOSI)
IMU_INT = Net("IMU_INT")
ENCODER_LEFT_ABI_A = Net("Encoder_Left_ABI_A")
ENCODER_LEFT_ABI_B = Net("Encoder_Left_ABI_B")
ENCODER_RIGHT_ABI_A = Net("Encoder_Right_ABI_A")
ENCODER_RIGHT_ABI_B = Net("Encoder_Right_ABI_B")

WALL_SENSOR_PWM_0 = Net("Wall_Sensor_PWM_0")
WALL_SENSOR_PWM_1 = Net("Wall_Sensor_PWM_1")
WALL_SENSOR_PWM_2 = Net("Wall_Sensor_PWM_2")
WALL_SENSOR_PWM_3 = Net("Wall_Sensor_PWM_3")
WALL_SENSOR_0 = Net("Wall_Sensor_0")
WALL_SENSOR_1 = Net("Wall_Sensor_1")
WALL_SENSOR_2 = Net("Wall_Sensor_2")
WALL_SENSOR_3 = Net("Wall_Sensor_3")
WALL_EMITTER_SET = Net("Wall_Emitter_Set")

MOTOR_LEFT_EN = Net("Motor_Left_EN")
MOTOR_LEFT_PH = Net("Motor_Left_PH")
MOTOR_RIGHT_EN = Net("Motor_Right_EN")
MOTOR_RIGHT_PH = Net("Motor_Right_PH")
MOTORS_ENABLE = Net("Motors_Enable")
MOTORS_NFAULT = Net("Motors_nFault")
MOTOR_L_SENSE_P = Net("Motor_L_Sense+")
MOTOR_L_SENSE_N = Net("Motor_L_Sense-")
MOTOR_R_SENSE_P = Net("Motor_R_Sense+")
MOTOR_R_SENSE_N = Net("Motor_R_Sense-")
CURRENT_SENSOR_LEFT = Net("Current_Sensor_Left")
CURRENT_SENSOR_RIGHT = Net("Current_Sensor_Right")

FAN_PWM = Net("Fan_PWM")
FAN_ENABLE = Net("Fan_Enable")
FAN_TOFF = Net("Fan_TOFF")

BATTERY_VOLTAGE = Net("Battery_Voltage")

# MCU.
STM32H725RGV6(
    name="IC1",
    paste="split",  # open thermal vias in the exposed pad: its paste in windows round them
    VDD=V3V3_D,
    VDDSMPS=V3V3_D,
    VDDA=VDDA,
    VBAT=V3V3_D,
    VLXSMPS=SMPS_LX,
    VFBSMPS=VCORE,
    VCAP1=VCORE,
    VCAP2=VCORE,
    VCAP3=VCORE,
    GND=GND,
    NRST=RESET,
    BOOT0=BOOT,
    PA0=ENCODER_LEFT_ABI_A,
    PA1=ENCODER_LEFT_ABI_B,
    PA2=BUZZER,
    PA3=ENCODER_LEFT_SPI.CS,
    PA4=WALL_SENSOR_0,
    PA5=WALL_EMITTER_SET,
    PA6=WALL_SENSOR_2,
    PA7=BUTTON,
    PA8=MOTOR_RIGHT_EN,
    PA9=ESP_FLOW,
    PA10=MOTORS_ENABLE,
    PA11=ESP_CSN,
    PA12=ESP_SCK,
    PA13=SWDIO,
    PA14=SWCLK,
    PA15=ENCODER_RIGHT_ABI_B,
    PB0=WALL_SENSOR_PWM_1,
    PB1=CURRENT_SENSOR_LEFT,
    PB2=MOTORS_NFAULT,
    PB3=ENCODER_RIGHT_ABI_A,
    PB4=WALL_SENSOR_PWM_2,
    PB5=WALL_SENSOR_PWM_3,
    PB6=IMU_INT,
    PB7=ENCODER_RIGHT_SPI.CS,
    PB8=MOTOR_RIGHT_PH,
    PB9=LED_ARGB,
    PB10=FAN_ENABLE,
    PB12=LED_RED,
    PB13=FAN_TOFF,
    PB14=ESP_DATA,
    PB15=FAN_PWM,
    PC0=WALL_SENSOR_3,
    PC1=CURRENT_SENSOR_RIGHT,
    PC4=WALL_SENSOR_1,
    PC5=BATTERY_VOLTAGE,
    PC6=MOTOR_LEFT_PH,
    PC7=MOTOR_LEFT_EN,
    PC9=WALL_SENSOR_PWM_0,
    PC10=SPI_SCK,
    PC11=SPI_MISO,
    PC12=SPI_MOSI,
    PC14=SWITCH_3,
    PC15=SWITCH_2,
    PD2=IMU_SPI.CS,
    PH0=SWITCH_0,
    PH1=SWITCH_1,
)

Capacitor(name="C1", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_10U_0603)
Capacitor(name="C2", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_4U7_0402)
AFE201612S2R2MBT(name="L1", P1=VCORE, P2=SMPS_LX)
Capacitor(name="C3", P1=GND, P2=VCORE, **C_10U_0603)
Capacitor(name="C4", P1=GND, P2=VCORE, **C_10U_0603)
Capacitor(name="C7", P1=GND, P2=VCORE, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C6", P1=GND, P2=VCORE, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C5", P1=GND, P2=VCORE, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C8", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C9", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_1U_0402)
Resistor(name="R67", P1=V3V3_A, P2=VDDA, **R_0_0402)
Capacitor(name="C10", P1=GND, P2=VDDA, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C11", P1=GND, P2=VDDA, **C_1U_0402)
Capacitor(name="C12", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C13", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C14", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C15", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C16", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C17", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_4U7_0402)

# SWD header for an ST-Link (bare pads, not assembled), a clone ST-Link's order: 1 SWDIO, 2 GND,
# 3 SWCLK, 4 its 5 V pin.
SwdHeader(name="SWD", prefix="SWD", supply=True, GND=GND, SWDIO=SWDIO, SWCLK=SWCLK, VDD=V5V_IN)

# M2 screw holes to the chassis.
MountingHole(name="H1")
MountingHole(name="H2")
MountingHole(name="H3")
MountingHole(name="H4")

Regulators(
    name="REGULATORS",
    BAT_P=BAT_P,
    VBAT=VBAT,
    V5V_IN=V5V_IN,
    VSYS=VSYS,
    V3V3_D=V3V3_D,
    V3V3_A=V3V3_A,
    GND=GND,
    GND_BAT=GND_BAT,
    Battery_Voltage=BATTERY_VOLTAGE,
)

Drivers(
    name="DRIVERS",
    VBAT=VBAT,
    V3V3_D=V3V3_D,
    GND=GND,
    Motor_Right_EN=MOTOR_RIGHT_EN,
    Motor_Right_PH=MOTOR_RIGHT_PH,
    Motor_Left_EN=MOTOR_LEFT_EN,
    Motor_Left_PH=MOTOR_LEFT_PH,
    Motors_Enable=MOTORS_ENABLE,
    Motors_nFault=MOTORS_NFAULT,
    MOTOR_R_SENSE_P=MOTOR_R_SENSE_P,
    MOTOR_R_SENSE_N=MOTOR_R_SENSE_N,
    MOTOR_L_SENSE_P=MOTOR_L_SENSE_P,
    MOTOR_L_SENSE_N=MOTOR_L_SENSE_N,
    Fan_PWM=FAN_PWM,
    Fan_Enable=FAN_ENABLE,
    Fan_TOFF=FAN_TOFF,
)

Sensors(
    name="SENSORS",
    V3V3_D=V3V3_D,
    V3V3_A=V3V3_A,
    GND=GND,
    SPI_SCK=SPI_SCK,
    SPI_MISO=SPI_MISO,
    SPI_MOSI=SPI_MOSI,
    IMU_SPI_CSn=IMU_SPI.CS,
    Encoder_Right_CSn=ENCODER_RIGHT_SPI.CS,
    Encoder_Left_CSn=ENCODER_LEFT_SPI.CS,
    IMU_INT=IMU_INT,
    MOTOR_L_SENSE_P=MOTOR_L_SENSE_P,
    MOTOR_L_SENSE_N=MOTOR_L_SENSE_N,
    MOTOR_R_SENSE_P=MOTOR_R_SENSE_P,
    MOTOR_R_SENSE_N=MOTOR_R_SENSE_N,
    Current_Sensor_Left=CURRENT_SENSOR_LEFT,
